          "topic": "Car-free Saturdays in the town centre",
          "lines": [
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker A",
              "text": "Good evening and welcome to City Talk. Tonight we ask whether the town centre should ban cars on Saturdays."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker B",
              "text": "Thanks for having me. Footfall on the high street rose by twelve per cent during the trial in May."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker C",
              "text": "That is true, but deliveries were late and two bakeries closed early on every Saturday of the trial."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker A",
              "text": "So the shops gained visitors but lost time?"
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker B",
              "text": "Mostly, yes. The cafes did best."
            },
            {
              "speaker": "Speaker C",
              "text": "And the bus routes need changing before anything is permanent."
            }
          ]
